From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] conpty: a terminal's own conpty.dll runs over Wine's pseudo consoles (7003)

Terminals ship conpty.dll (Windows Terminal; node-pty, so VS Code and
other Electron terminals). Their copy starts OpenConsole.exe on the
kernel's console driver (\Device\ConDrv\Server), which Wine does not
have: VS Code's integrated terminal failed with "Cannot launch conpty".
A builtin conpty.dll, preferred over the program's copy by a default
override in wine.inf (HKLM\Software\Wine\DllOverrides conpty=builtin),
keeps its calls on kernelbase's pseudo console: create, resize, clear,
show/hide, reparent, release, close (also with a timeout), pack. conhost
reads the clear, show/hide and reparent signals: a clear drops the
buffer but the cursor's line, so a repaint does not draw what the
terminal cleared; show/hide and reparent are read whole and otherwise
ignored, a pseudo console having no window.
---
